```

**Manual Testing Checklist:**

Each micro-frontend module must complete this accessibility checklist before production deployment:

**Keyboard Navigation:**
- [ ] All interactive elements accessible via Tab key
- [ ] Tab order follows logical reading order (top to bottom, left to right)
- [ ] Enter/Space activate buttons and links
- [ ] Escape closes modals and dismisses overlays
- [ ] Arrow keys navigate within components (dropdowns, tabs, carousels)
- [ ] No keyboard traps—users can navigate into and out of all modules

**Screen Reader Compatibility:**
- [ ] Module transitions announced correctly in JAWS (Windows + Chrome)
- [ ] Module transitions announced correctly in NVDA (Windows + Firefox)
- [ ] Module transitions announced correctly in VoiceOver (macOS + Safari)
- [ ] Loading states announced via `role="status"` and `aria-live="polite"`
- [ ] Error states announced immediately via `role="alert"` and `aria-live="assertive"`
- [ ] All images have descriptive `alt` text (or `alt=""` for decorative images)
- [ ] Form inputs have associated `<label>` elements or `aria-label` attributes
- [ ] Dynamic content changes announced appropriately

**Focus Management:**
- [ ] Focus visible with clear indicator (2px outline, high contrast)
- [ ] Focus indicator meets 3:1 contrast ratio against background (WCAG 2.2 AA)
- [ ] Focus moves logically when module loads/unloads
- [ ] Focus returns to triggering element when closing modals
- [ ] Skip links allow bypassing navigation to main content

**Color and Contrast:**
- [ ] Normal text (< 18pt) meets 4.5:1 contrast ratio
- [ ] Large text (≥ 18pt or ≥ 14pt bold) meets 3:1 contrast ratio
- [ ] Interactive elements (buttons, links) have 3:1 contrast against adjacent colors
- [ ] Color not sole means of conveying information (use icons, labels, patterns)

**Responsive and Zoom:**
- [ ] Interface usable at 200% zoom without horizontal scrolling
- [ ] Text reflows without overlapping at 400% zoom
- [ ] All functionality available on mobile devices with touch and screen readers

**Forms and Inputs:**
- [ ] All form fields have visible labels
- [ ] Required fields indicated with `aria-required="true"` and visible indicator
- [ ] Error messages associated with fields via `aria-describedby`
- [ ] Error messages include clear instructions for correction

**Module-Specific Concerns:**
- [ ] Loading indicators visible and announced during lazy module loading
- [ ] Error boundaries provide accessible retry mechanism
- [ ] Cross-module navigation preserves focus context
- [ ] Shared dependencies (design system) maintain consistent accessibility patterns

